Moonsilence wrote:
>
> 1. What is the difference between stealth and invisibility?

Sound and vision.  Without stealth your movements make sound.
Invisibility has the problem that some monsters see invisible
and others see heat.

> 3. Does it make a diffenece if my pet attacks peaceful/tame monsters?

There is no punishment when your pet kills a peacefull.

> For example, if I play an orcish char, the game promts me wether I
> really want to attack the o. My pet just does... How can I make him
> stop doing that? He even attacks watchmen in mine town.

The watchmen are sources of good equipment at that point so you
don't want to stop them.  The watch captain can give the best
non-artifact weapon up to that point in some games.  Shopkeepers
have money and other items.  The only ones you don't want your
pet to kill are Iszak and the co-aligned temple priest.  If your pet
starts attacking the watch captain there's risk of it attacking the
shopkeepers so decide to stay or leave then.

